**/outputs/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.avi
*.flv
*.wmv
*.m4v

# NOTE: image types are deliberately NOT blanket-ignored. This project has no
# render/cache directories at all (verified), so all 4,741 local .png files are
# UI icons and DSPy evaluation frames that belong in git. Blanket-ignoring
# *.png would silently drop them, and .gitignore cannot express "only if the
# parent is named outputs" because negation cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded.
# If you later create a render output directory, add it to the block above and
# keep its images out via directory name, not by extension.

# --- Live runtime state (rewritten on a timer by resident services) ------------
# local_agent/runtime/ is a live working directory: resident services rewrite gate
# JSON every 15-30s, and active Claude Code sessions write render output, logs and
# eval frames into it continuously. Tracking it produces noisy diffs and races
# `git add` (files disappear mid-index). Treat the whole tree as generated state;
# all authored source, docs, CHANGELOGs and tests live outside it.
local_agent/runtime/
**/local_agent/runtime/

**/file_edit_gate.json
**/gpu_gate.json
worker_farm/farm_status.json
**/farm_status.json
worker_farm/runtime/
**/watcher_owner.json
**/image_render_owner.json
**/batch_render_queue_owner.json

# Atomic-write temp files. Services write state via "name.json.<rand>.tmp" then
# rename it into place. Git can list one and find it already gone, which aborts
# `git add -A` with "unable to index file". Matches .k5gul5d4.tmp and friends.
*.tmp
*.tmp.*
**/*.json.*.tmp
**/*.json.tmp

# --- Regenerable build/test artifacts (rebuilt, not source) -------------------
# Excluded so the first commit stays a usable size instead of a 1.5GB dump.
# DSPy evaluation frames are regenerated by optimize/evaluate_dspy_pipeline.py.
**/dspy_opt/
**/dspy_opt/**
# Local backup snapshots written before each patch/unattended edit.
*.bak_*
*.bak

# --- Runtime/staging directories (external clones, GPU scratch, temp work) -----
external/
artifacts/
live_jobs/
# work/ (blanket rule retired 2026-11: source in work/ is tracked, see end of file)
comfy_output/
run/
tmp/
scratch/
**/uploads/derived/
**/managed_tasks/

# --- Vendored trees unreadable by this account (CodexSandboxOnline ACLs) -------
# local_agent/vendor/LXMF, RNS, serial, CRNS, bin and three dist-info folders
# deny 'rhine' read access, so Git silently skips them. Excluding the tree makes
# that gap explicit rather than invisible. Repairing the ACLs needs an admin.
local_agent/vendor/
**/local_agent/vendor/

# --- Third-party clones with their own git remotes ----------------------------
# Git would record these as broken gitlinks (mode 160000): a fresh clone gets an
# empty directory instead of code, because their remotes are unrelated public
# repos. Re-clone them where needed rather than tracking them here.
local_agent/vendor_sideband
**/vendor_sideband/
**/gvd_qa/quarantine/

